 (tunits punits units)←MyUnits object;units;ppxsize;pscale;scale;pxsize;parent
⍝ Determine what pixel-size my object's (and my parent's, and all the system's) unit sizes are

 parent←⊃object._Ancestry,##.##.GUIroot
 :While 0≠parent.⎕NC'_Owner' ⋄ parent←parent._Owner ⋄ :EndWhile ⍝ Find logical parent
 ((scale pxsize)(pscale ppxsize))←(object,parent)⎕VGET('_scale' 1)('_pix_size'(0 0))
 punits←units←##.##.GUIroot._units ⍝ Get system conversion factors
 tunits←object ⎕VGET⊂'_units'punits ⍝ Watch for local override (for Printers)
 tunits←(tunits⍪⍨pxsize÷1⌈|2↑3↓scale)[1+⊃scale;] ⍝ Compute unit-conversions for this object's scale ⍝? Is this anywhere close to right for scale=0??
 punits←(punits⍪⍨ppxsize÷1⌈|2↑3↓pscale)[1+⊃pscale;] ⍝ Compute unit-conversions for the parent object's scale

 ⍝? Note: We might need to use ∆Border for some of these calculations?? Or won't it matter?
